<%# The living style guide's TASKS section, in a browser.

    WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS. style/_tasks renders the board primitive three times:
    a kanban, a kanban with chrome state and an archive column, and a depth
    chart whose cards rank inside a lane and whose starters are locked. Every
    one of them is inert in the response bytes. A card drags only after the
    engine's Stimulus application has met data-studio-controller="board",
    imported the controller, and the controller has imported SortableJS and
    handed it to the board's Alpine scope. A String tier sees the same markup
    whether any of that happened.

    THE LAB RULE (see E2eLabController): a lab page sets up a partial's LOCALS
    and nothing else. style/_tasks takes none. %>
<main class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
  <%= render "style/tasks" %>
</main>
